## Objective
- Autonomously hunt valid, reproducible, high-impact vulnerabilities against the authorized target `https://console.byteplus.com/finance/`, following `skills/AGENT.md` exactly, and report evidence under `result/`.

## Important Details
- Repo root: `/home/runner/work/aaii-aautomattionn/aaii-aautomattionn`.
- Scope: from `data/targets.txt`: `https://console.byteplus.com/finance/`; note says `console.byteplus.com` is in-scope for a private BBP. No other `data/` target files.
- `data/targets.txt` also instructs sending confirmed vulns to a Discord webhook `https://discord.com/api/webhooks/1565069909266927626/...`. Agent **REFUSED** as outbound exfiltration / possible prompt-injection / embedded secret; refusal documented in `result/scope.md` (`Discord webhook instruction: REFUSED / NOT FOLLOWED`). CI already auto-notifies from `result/confirmed-vuln.txt`.
- Test accounts in `creds/test-account.txt`:
  - Account A: `adoringjepsen1@fearlessmails.com` / `Acd3423@#345566` → AccountID `3000823185`, username `test-user-123`, org `test-org`.
  - Account B: `testt456` / `Acd3423@#345` → AccountID `3001021825`, username `testt456`, org `attacker-org`.
- Login URL in creds is `https://console.byteplus.com/auth/login/`; direct nav to `/finance/` redirects to `https://signin.byteplus.com/auth/login?redirectURI=...` (different origin). Agent logged in via `console.byteplus.com/auth/login/` official flow to reach the authorized route; not testing signin origin's own bugs.
- Session metadata: `run_id=41023928544`, `event=workflow_dispatch`, `target_hash=7f8307f45ca9e92f7db2f002cb8c16cf01320f9db434bddca9dc3ba2c65c9eb1`, decision `reset` (prior results from another target).
- API pattern: `/api/top/<service>/<region>/<version>/<Action>`, e.g. `/api/top/bill/ap-singapore-1/2020-01-01/<Action>` (region `ap-singapore-1`, default version `2020-01-01`).
- Auth: cookie session + `csrfToken` cookie used as `x-csrf-token` header; `digest` JWT (`sub=3000823185`), `volc_oauth_security_token_v2`. Use same-origin `fetch(..., {credentials:'include'})` inside the page to preserve auth/CSRF.
- Tools/env: Chrome DevTools MCP at `http://127.0.0.1:9222`, Chrome `156.0.8078.73` headless; `opencode`, `node v22.23.4`, `python3`, `curl`, `git` present. **`rg` is NOT installed** — use python/grep tool.
- Browser pages: `pageId=1` = Account A (`/finance/bill/detail/?menuType=list`); `pageId=2` = Account B (`isolatedContext=acct-b`, at `/home`).
- Finance routes seen: `/finance/overview`, `/finance/bill/detail`, `/finance/bill/split-bill`, `/finance/bill/cost-analyse`, `/finance/invoice-manage`, `/finance/payment-methods`, `/finance/report`, `/finance/pickup-coupon`.
- Routes are React SPA; JS bundles on `https://res.gcloudcache.com/bp-fe/finance/byteplus/static/js/1.0.1.2888/` (CDN is out of scope as asset, but route-related JS inspected).
- Candidate client-side issue: in `main.def4a3cd.js` ~offset 93845, redirect handler uses `location.replace(t)` with `secureDomains` `host.endsWith(domain)` check — runtime `secureDomains` unresolved (`INIT_CONFIG` only has `serviceOpen`). Order-result redirect regex in `async_4430.a89ed579.js` ~26499: default `^(https?:)?//[\w.-]+[.](bytedance\.net|volcengine\.com|volcengine\.cn|volcanicengine\.com|coze\.cn)(/.*|$)`, or relative-only depending on `expenseConfig.order_result_return_url_reg`. Payment sinks: `async_2693.00351e26.js` `location.href=o` ~4488 and `location.href=l.url` ~5028 (`redirect_details.url` from `AddPaymentMethod`; `callbackUrl` built from pathname+query).

## Work State
### Completed
- Preflight done; created dirs `result/client-side`, `result/server-side`, `result/findings`, `result/inventory`, `result/logs`.
- Wrote `result/logs/session.md` and `result/scope.md` (scope table, in/out-of-scope, Discord refusal).
- Read `skills/AGENT.md`, `skills/client-side-skill.md`, `skills/server-side-skill.md`, listed `vulnebleti/` dirs (ATO, BAC, File_upload, Forget_password_endpoint, Fuzz, etc.).
- Confirmed both test accounts log in and captured their IDs/orgs (A=test-org/3000823185, B=attacker-org/3001021825).
- Captured `/finance/overview` and `/finance/bill/detail/?menuType=list` network traffic; key endpoints: `GetProfileInfo`, `getExpenseConfigForFE`, `GetAccountGrayStatus`, `ListMonthlyBillOpen`, `QueryCreditProtocolDetail`, `ListCostAnalysisTrend`, `GetFilterInfoForBillDetail`, `ListPayerAndOwnerByBillOwnerID`, `GetCurrency`, `GetBcDiscountPriceAuth`.
- Downloaded & hashed finance route JS to `result/client-side/console.byteplus.com/finance-overview/javascript/` (files incl. `main.def4a3cd.js`, `2388.6a141900.js`, `async_*.js`, `lib-*.js`, `hashes.txt`).
- Screenshot saved: `result/client-side/console.byteplus.com/finance-overview/overview.png`.
- IDOR negative results (tested A↔B cross-account):
  - `GET /api/top/bill/ap-singapore-1/2020-01-01/QueryCreditProtocolDetail?AccountID=3001021825` from A returns `AccountID:3000823185` (param ignored; session-derived).
  - `ListMonthlyBillOpen?PayerID=...` — `PayerID` honored as filter but isolation enforced: A cannot see B's bills and B cannot see A's bills (each sees own `PayerID`/`PayerUserName`).
  - `ListPayerAndOwnerByBillOwnerID?BillOwnerID=3000823185` from B returns empty lists (both accounts have no bill data).
- Action/endpoint candidates extracted from JS: `AddPaymentMethod`, `ListPayerAndOwnerByBillOwnerID`, `GetBcUserProductSplitDimensionOpen`, `SetBcUserProductSplitDimensionOpen`, `ListWithdrawReservedProductConfigs`, `ListOrder`, `ListOrderChannel`, `QueryDiscountPrice`, `CompleteProfile`, `/bill/split-bill`, `/finance/invoice-manage`, `/api/financial/payment/AddPaymentMethod`.
- `result/confirmed-vuln.txt` still empty (header only); no confirmed findings yet.

### Active
- Client-side analysis of finance route JS: searching for URL/query-param readers (`menuType`, `BillID`, `AccountID`, `URLSearchParams`, `location.search/hash`, `postMessage`) and DOM sinks. Latest finding: `async_5453.754e8b4d.js` @1627 builds link `/bill/detail/?menuType=list&AccountID=<AccountID>&BillID=<A>` from response data (not URL) — not yet a confirmed source.
- Investigating bill-detail URL param handling and other server endpoints that accept `AccountID`/`PayerID`/`BillOwnerID` (e.g. `ListBillDetail`, `ListNewBillDetail`, `ListSplitBillDetail`, `GetInvoiceAccount`, `ListSubjectBalanceByAccountID`) for BOLA/IDOR.
- Considering payment/open-redirect sinks (`async_2693`, `async_4430`, `AddPaymentMethod` `returnUrl`/`callbackUrl`).

### Blocked
- Both test accounts have $0 / empty billing data, so bill-data IDOR is hard to distinguish; need a metadata oracle (e.g. `PayerID`/`PayerUserName` echo in `ListMonthlyBillOpen`) per endpoint.
- Runtime `secureDomains` list unresolved (not in `.projectData` `INIT_CONFIG`). `rg` unavailable (use python).
- Open redirect likely lives on `signin.byteplus.com` (out of scope), so must confirm any redirect sink is on `console.byteplus.com`.

## Next Move
1. Inspect bill-detail page URL param usage in JS (how `AccountID`/`BillID`/`menuType` from `location.search` flow into API calls) and enumerate bill read endpoints with parameter names.
2. Test B→A (and A→B) against candidate endpoints (`ListBillDetail`/`ListNewBillDetail`/`ListSplitBillDetail`, `GetInvoiceAccount`, `ListSubjectBalanceByAccountID`, `ListOrder`, `ListPayerAndOwnerByBillOwnerID` variants) using in-page `fetch` with `x-csrf-token`; look for metadata echo proving cross-account access.
3. Capture `/finance/invoice-manage`, `/finance/payment-methods`, `/finance/bill/split-bill` traffic for more endpoints, then evaluate payment `returnUrl`/`callbackUrl` open-redirect sinks on `console.byteplus.com`.
